---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — Mohd Bilal | Academy of Korean Studies"
  description="Researcher of Hallyu in India and India–Korea exchange. Master's student in Korean Studies at the Academy of Korean Studies; builds corpora, networks, and datasets for cultural history."
>
  <section class="band container">
    <h1 class="display-md rise">About</h1>

    <div class="prose about-lede">
      <p class="body-lg rise rise-2">
        I study how Korea and India read each other. That single question runs through
        everything on this site: how Indian newspapers frame the Korean Wave, how
        Buddhist monks and scholars moved between the two countries across centuries,
        and how kisaeng wrote about their own lives in a 1927 Seoul magazine.
      </p>
      <p class="body-md rise rise-3">
        I work on these questions computationally. Rather than reading a handful of
        sources closely and stopping there, I build the full corpus first — thousands
        of newspaper articles, a network of historical mediators, a digitized magazine —
        and then ask what patterns hold across all of it. The projects on this site are
        that method in practice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container"><hr class="hr" /></div>

  <section class="band container reveal">
    <h2 class="display-sm">Background</h2>
    <div class="prose section-body">
      <p class="body-md">
        I'm from India, and I came to Korean Studies from that side of the exchange.
        I hold a BA in Korean Studies and I'm now a Master's student at the Academy of
        Korean Studies in South Korea, where my research sits between Hallyu studies,
        cultural history, and digital humanities.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container"><hr class="hr" /></div>

  <section class="band container reveal">
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <h2 class="display-sm">Languages</h2>
        <ul class="fact-list body-md">
          <li>English — fluent</li>
          <li>Hindi/Urdu — native</li>
          <li>Korean — working research proficiency</li>
          <li>Hanja-mixed and classical texts — reading ability</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="display-sm">Tools</h2>
        <p class="body-md section-body">
          Python for corpus work and analysis; SQLite and DuckDB for corpus storage;
          Kiwi for Korean tokenization; network analysis for the historical projects;
          Astro for this site.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container"><hr class="hr" /></div>

  <section class="band container reveal">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="body-md cta-line">
        For the formal record — education, skills, and everything in one document —
      </p>
      <a class="pill pill--filled" href="/cv">Read my CV →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .about-lede {
      margin-top: var(--s-2xl);
    }

    .section-body {
      margin-top: var(--s-lg);
    }

    .section-body p,
    p.section-body {
      margin: 0;
    }

    .two-col {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--s-3xl);
    }

    @media (max-width: 767px) {
      .two-col {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }

    .fact-list {
      list-style: none;
      margin: var(--s-lg) 0 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--s-md);
    }

    .fact-list li {
      padding-bottom: var(--s-md);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    }

    .fact-list li:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }

    .cta-line {
      margin: 0 0 var(--s-lg);
    }
  </style>
</Base>
